- For $X = {0} union [1, 2]$, the point $0$ is isolated while every point of $[1, 2]$ is an accumulation point of $X$.

- Every point of the circle $S = {z in CC: |z| = 1}$ is an accumulation point of the disc $D = {z in CC: |z| < 1}$.

- All points of $D = {z in CC: |z| < 1}$ are accumulation points of $D$, and the same holds for the closed set ${|z| <= 1}$.
